A||||13||Adrift||Steering Wheel Replacements from other cars - what fits?||||1||
Z||000000||Adrift||06-29-2001||12:04 PM||||I am going to a yard today and was wondering if there are any cars I should look out for which I can grab a steering wheel from - How does a steering wheel hookup to a car anyways? How do you go about removing one?||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||06-29-2001||01:27 PM||||you pop off the horn button. then you will see the end of the shaft with a large nut on it. There is a clip sort of shaped like a 'C' in a groove that keeps it from backing off. Pop off the clip- take off the nut-then you need a steering wheel or gear puller to pop it loose. Id get an aftermarket wheel instead of off a wrecked car. Grant wheels has them from $20 up. I have a really nice leather wrapped Grant for $29. If you want better- MOMOs are around $150 & up.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||stsmithgt||06-29-2001||04:01 PM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driversid1_2.jpg">   Mine is a Grant wheel(signature series), but it was over $150.  Almost $200 with the adapter.  The shop I bought it from isn't the cheapest place around, "Tognotti's auto world" in Sacramento.  Ergonomic wheels are cool.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Dang, I see now my speaker covers really stand out, I need to darken them up. jeez!<p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 06-29-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000003||kinboyatuwo||06-29-2001||04:25 PM||||hey stsmithgt, did the same thing and it looks good, did mine years ago and an ex girlfriend coulndt drive when it was sunny, she was short and the reflection obstructed her view<BR>so two reasons to do it<BR>beauty and accident prevention (she was not that great a driver<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/kinboyatuwo/kinboyatuwo.jpg">    <BR>"Friends don't let friends drive four doors."<P>87 Duke, 235,000km||||reg||6
