Z||000006||DXR_DAD||06-29-2001||10:34 PM||||Don't feel bad stsmithgt that price is about right! Another Grant (Signature) $150.00+ Carbon Fiber   With out center cap<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723595&p=35730469&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P><BR>Same wheel with center cap:<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723595&p=21451557&Sequence=2&res=high"> <P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||3
Z||000007||DXR_DAD||06-29-2001||10:38 PM||||Adrift, it's just Fit, Feel, Looks and how much you want to spend!! So it's all about what you want.....and that makes a good wheel<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||3
Z||000008||filthyscarecrow||06-30-2001||07:10 PM||||i have a momo mod31 on mine. i used to have a grant formula GT which was really nice, but doesn't compare to the momo. it feels better in my hands, and that means better communication between the road and your hands. i still have the grant wheel, which i'd sell if anyone were interested. i have a custom aluminum hub for it and it looks stock. the wheel is a bit small though at 11.75 inches. it feels great, but john q law might not care what it feels like when he writes you a ticket. i like the momo wheels though because the suede covered race wheels come undrilled, so you can drill it to fit any hub that you already have. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||johnt671||07-01-2001||08:26 AM||||I put a Grant Signature in mine for $70 + the kit .  It is a smaller diameter the the original, which makes it easier to get in and out of the car, and nice and thick.  Wrapped in black leather.||||reg||1
Z||000010||artherd||07-01-2001||03:01 PM||||On a side note, I really like the wheel in newer Audi A4s.  No idea if it will even come close to fit, and it's an airbag wheel, so probally expensive.<P>But it'd sure be cool. I might have to try it someday.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000011||stimpy||07-01-2001||03:34 PM||||Do aftermarket wheels sit closer to you then stock wheels? ||||reg||1
Z||000012||stsmithgt||07-02-2001||10:58 AM||||The adapter does make the steering wheel a little closer, but I like it that way.  I also like the smaller wheel diameter.  The stock one would drag on my legs with the wheel positioned where I felt comfortable steering it and this new one doesn't drag at all.  The "D" shape gives me a <I>litte</I> more room to shuffle my legs around on long trips without banging into the wheel too.  I'm glad I'm not the only nut to pay over 150.00 bucks out there for a steering wheel. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||Philphine||07-02-2001||11:13 AM||||i've been seeing a wheel called dotta in the nopi adds. about $130 and d-shaped also. anyone know about them?<P>as far as factory wheels i think i'd like to have one of those pontiac wheels wih the radio controls to experiment with.||||reg||1
